Plugin I/O, part four: self-signed TLS.

fetch and WebSocket.connect take tls: { pin: "sha256/<hex>" } (the SHA-256
of the server's DER certificate, colons allowed) or { insecure: true }. Both
skip chain and hostname checks; the handshake signature is still verified.
One tls module builds every rustls config with the ring provider explicitly,
and wss now trusts the system roots, as fetch already did. With tls set,
fetch refuses cross-origin redirects; tls with unix is an error.

